{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929","id":"msg_01DLcHjWt5dRz5fLuAFMjJpF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Aha! The uncommitted changes show that STORY-001 and STORY-002 were previously marked as `passes: true`, but the current state shows them as `passes: false`. This means the changes were never committed.\n\nLooking at the context, I now understand the situation:\n1. Previous iterations implemented STORY-001 and STORY-002\n2. They updated prd.json to mark them as complete (`passes: true`)\n3. But those updates to prd.json were never committed\n4. The backpressure hook (quality checks) likely failed, causing the iteration to exit\n5. Since the prd.json changes weren't committed, they persist as uncommitted changes\n\nThe right thing to do now is to:\n1. Run the quality checks to see what's actually failing\n2. Fix any errors\n3. Commit the proper state\n\nBut first, let me understand what the actual error was by checking if Docker can start:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":712,"cache_read_input_tokens":82047,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":712},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1b7bd4eb-0958-4b68-b261-13555ff4861d","uuid":"ace1c557-7275-4a39-96fd-0a1b458d38ad"}
